        "title": "Explore Split in a classifier",
        "subtitle": "Separate an array into ordered parts with chosen sizes.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How the sample directions work",
        "formula": "Separate an array into ordered parts with chosen sizes.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A tensor is an array with named directions. A sample is one observation; a batch is a group of observations. Sample direction selects where to cut each observation; the observation direction always stays separate. A negative direction counts backward; \u22121 means the last direction.",
          "Choose Equal-sized parts to set Split size, or Chosen section sizes to enter each positive Section size in order. Chosen sizes must add up to the selected direction. Equal sizes may leave a smaller final part. The inactive setting resets to its default.",
          "Each actual part has its own connector, named part0, part1 and onward in source order. At most eight parts are supported. A connector exists only when its part exists. If changed settings remove a connected part, repair the highlighted connection; it is never silently redirected.",
          "Inspect the different part tables and reconnect them with Concatenate. In the two measured lessons, rebuild the requested order and check how a small source change affects the result."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open Split example",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/TensorRoutingWorkflowExample.swift",
        "lessonIDs": [
          "assessment.split-size-order",
          "assessment.split-sections-order"
        ]
      }
