        "updatedAt": "2026-10-08",
        "exampleID": "prepared-gather-classifier",
        "sourceResource": "workflow-observations",
        "title": "Explore Gather in a classifier",
        "subtitle": "Choose source values by their exact positions.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How the sample directions work",
        "formula": "Choose source values by their exact positions.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "An array is a table of values extended across named directions. Source carries measured values; Indices carries whole-number positions starting at zero. A sample is one observation; a batch groups observations. Both inputs keep the same observation count and number of directions.",
          "Sample direction tells the block where each position applies. Other selector directions may be smaller than their source directions; they are not repeated automatically. Negative or out-of-range positions are refused.",
          "Selecting the same source position several times repeats that value. Input influence means how a small source change affects the result; repeated selections add their influences together. Position numbers are choices, not trainable measurements, so they receive no influence values.",
          "The example connects MaxPool1d winning positions to Gather. The lesson uses supplied position arrays and checks selected values and independent source influence. Private assessment positions and answers remain hidden."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open Gather example",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/TensorRoutingWorkflowExample.swift",
        "lessonIDs": [
          "assessment.gather-repeated-positions"
        ]
