        "updatedAt": "2026-10-08",
        "exampleID": "prepared-einsum-classifier",
        "sourceResource": "workflow-observations",
        "title": "Explore Einsum in a classifier",
        "subtitle": "Combine or rearrange arrays using named arrangements.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How the sample directions work",
        "formula": "Combine or rearrange arrays using named arrangements.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "An array has named directions; a sample is one observation and a batch is a group of observations. Arrangement preset offers familiar operations without entering notation: Combine tables, Pair each value, Read a diagonal, or Swap sample directions.",
          "Combine tables uses sources A and B. Read a diagonal and Swap sample directions use only A. Configured connectors show the actual sources required by the chosen arrangement. For more than two sources, use another block; this block accepts at most two.",
          "Advanced Custom notation names directions with ASCII letters and an explicit arrow showing the output. The letter n always names observations and stays first on both sides; it cannot be combined, repeated or moved. Matching sample letters match sizes or reuse a size-one direction; repeated letters inside one source select a diagonal.",
          "Custom notation is a bounded description of array directions, never executable code. Spaces are allowed; implicit outputs and ellipses are not. Work is bounded before running. The measured lessons compare combined tables and a diagonal, including how small source changes affect each result."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open Einsum example",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/TensorRoutingWorkflowExample.swift",
